INC4_TODO=THE ACTUAL B1. (1) Demux::Fmp4 variant in crate (lib.rs:547 enum + fill_queues + do_seek arms). KEY STRUCTURAL DIFF: DASH video+audio are SEPARATE segment streams (unlike MP4/MKV 1-file-both-tracks) -> Demux::Fmp4 holds TWO fragmented sources (video reader -> VFrame H264, audio reader -> AFrame AAC), fill_queues pulls both. (2) fMP4 = ftyp+moov(init)+[moof+mdat]* so concat(init, media segs) = valid fragmented MP4 -> feed mp4::Mp4Reader (proven repros/fmp4-probe). Need a segment reader (HttpRangeReader is single-contiguous-file; DASH=init+N segment URLs). MVP option: streaming append-buffer per rep (Cursor over growing Vec, bounded prefetch). (3) dash-app driver: dash-mpd parse -> pick 1 video+1 audio Representation -> resolve init+media seg URLs (SegmentTemplate/List/Timeline) -> open into Demux::Fmp4 -> install_player -> Phase::Playing. READ repros/fmp4-probe FIRST for exact fragmented mp4 API.

INC4_FINDING=⚠️ VERIFIED (read mp4 0.14 source): the task's "fMP4 PROVEN / no new demuxer" claim is FALSE + doc-only (repros/fmp4-probe is empty fn main(){}; commit bd892f17 changed only docs). mp4 0.14 PARSES fragment boxes (moofs/traf/trun/tfhd/tfdt exposed w/ sample_sizes/durations/cts/data_offset/base_media_decode_time) BUT read_sample() is BROKEN for CMAF: track.rs sample_offset() fragment path returns constant tfhd.base_data_offset.unwrap_or(0) (ignores sample idx, no trun.data_offset, no size accumulation, =0 when default-base-is-moof) -> garbage. So Demux::Fmp4 MUST hand-compute sample layout (moof_start+trun.data_offset+Σsizes; PTS=tfdt.base_media_decode_time+Σdurations+cts) reusing mp4 for box-parse only. CORRECTED task doc + saved memory reference_mp4_014_fragmented_read_sample_broken. Inc4 is now BIGGER than "wire mp4::read_sample".
INC4_DECISION_PENDING=approach for the fragmented reader + segment feed: (A) streaming hand-parse per-segment (parse each media seg's moof/trun as it arrives, bounded prefetch; enables real streaming; more code) vs (B) download-then-play MVP (fetch all segments of 1 video+1 audio rep into 2 buffers, concat init+segs, mp4::read_header for box tree + our offset math, Cursor feed; simpler/faster first proof; memory-heavy, not adaptive). Both need a play-test (visual, user). REPORTED to user for decision.

INC4_CRATE_CHECK=User asked to check for a more functional mp4 demuxer (oxideav-mp4 + others). RESULT: oxideav-mp4 0.0.9 is the WINNER. Verified by reading source + wasm build. Candidates: mp4ff=Go(skip); re_mp4=parser-only no fragmented; mp4box 0.12.1=correct fragmented offsets(ffprobe-matching) BUT track_samples_from_path=whole-file/path API (bad for HTTP streaming); oxideav-mp4 0.0.9=BEST. oxideav-mp4: ✅COMPILES wasm32-wasip2 (verified in repros/fmp4-probe); pure-Rust MIT; streaming Demuxer trait (oxideav-container) open(Box<dyn ReadSeek>,&CodecResolver)->next_packet()->Packet{stream_index,pts,dts,time_base,flags{keyframe,header,discard},data} + seek_to(tfra/sidx, fragment-BOUNDED linear fallback, NOT EOF-scan) + streams()->StreamInfo{time_base,params:CodecParameters{codec_id,media_type,sample_rate,channels,extradata}} + set_active_streams; handles progressive AND fragmented CMAF/DASH/HLS; oxideav ECOSYSTEM we already use (oxideav-core/oxideav-ac3). CAUTIONS: (1) reader must be Send - our HttpRangeReader uses Rc=!Send -> need Send wrapper (trivial, single-thread wasm); (2) 0.0.9 young -> pin EXACT like oxideav-ac3. => Demux::Fmp4 wraps Box<dyn oxideav_container::Demuxer>; DASH video+audio=2 demuxers (one per rep reader). BEATS vendor+patch mp4 0.14 and hand-parse-trun. fmp4-probe now has deps added (oxideav-mp4/container/core) - EMPIRICAL verify next: fetch real Tears-of-Steel init+seg, open+next_packet, confirm sane video keyframes/pts/extradata BEFORE wiring engine (humility: compiles != demuxes-correctly).

INC4_PROBE_PASS=✅ EMPIRICAL PROOF (repros/fmp4-probe, native run): oxideav-mp4 0.0.9 DEMUXES real Tears-of-Steel CMAF CORRECTLY. Concat(init ftyp+moov, media styp+moof+mdat) -> oxideav_mp4::demux::open(Box<dyn oxideav_core::ReadSeek>, &NullCodecResolver). VIDEO: codec h264, 224x100, extradata=52B valid avcC (01 42 c0 0d = Baseline/L13 matches manifest avc1.42C00D), pkt#0 IDR keyframe 1662B, PTS 0/25/50/.. tb=1/600 ~24fps, 96 pkts=4s, monotonic. AUDIO: codec aac sr48000 ch2, extradata=[11,90] ASC=AAC-LC/48k/stereo, PTS -2048/-1024/0/1024.. (priming+1024/frame), 188 pkts. Both PASS. Packet.data is AVCC length-prefixed (avcC lengthSizeMinusOne=ff -> nal_len=4) -> engine install_player already does AVCC->AnnexB. API: oxideav_container::Demuxer{streams()->[StreamInfo{params:CodecParameters{codec_id,media_type,width,height,sample_rate,channels,extradata}}], next_packet()->Packet{stream_index,pts:Option<i64>,dts,flags.keyframe,data:Vec<u8>}, seek_to, duration_micros}; Cursor<Vec<u8>> satisfies ReadSeek(Read+Seek+Send). => VALIDATED: build Demux::Fmp4 on oxideav-mp4 (pin =0.0.9). samples/ (4 .dash ~45KB) kept as probe fixtures.
INC4_NEXT=Wire Demux::Fmp4 in crate: variant holds 2 oxideav Demuxers (video rep reader + audio rep reader; DASH separates them); fill_queues Fmp4 arm = next_packet from each -> VFrame(video, nal_len=4 AVCC)/AFrame(audio AAC); do_seek arm = seek_to; install config from StreamInfo extradata (avcC->DecoderConfig; ASC->setup_aac_audio). Reader=Send wrapper over HttpRangeReader (Rc=!Send) OR feed download-then-play buffers (Cursor is Send) for first cut. dash-app driver: dash-mpd parse -> resolve init+media seg URLs (SegmentTemplate $RepresentationID$/$Time$ + SegmentTimeline; BaseURL=dash/) -> open Demux::Fmp4 -> install_player -> Playing.

